    "The timeline shows up when the scene has something to play: a key, an animated model, a simulation or a formula that uses the time (View > Timeline Bar changes that). Press the space bar to play. Right-click a parameter to key it: the diamonds on the ruler are its keys, and the line with a small triangle is the current frame.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The timeline shows up when the scene has something to play: a key, an animated model, a simulation or a formula that uses the time (View > Timeline Bar changes that). Press the space bar to play. Right-click a parameter to key it: the diamonds on the ruler are its keys, and the line with a small triangle is the current frame."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La chronologie apparaît quand la scène a quelque chose à lire : une image clé, un modèle animé, une simulation ou une formule qui utilise le temps (Présentation > Barre de chronologie permet de changer cela). Appuyez sur la barre d’espace pour lancer la lecture. Un clic droit sur un paramètre y pose une image clé : les losanges de la règle sont les images clés, et la ligne surmontée d’un petit triangle est l’image courante."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Export an image of the viewport with File > Export Image…, or the shown geometry as an OBJ file with File > Export Geometry….": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Export an image of the viewport with File > Export Image…, or the shown geometry as an OBJ file with File > Export Geometry…."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fichier > Exporter l’image… enregistre une image de la vue 3D, et Fichier > Exporter la géométrie… écrit la géométrie affichée dans un fichier OBJ."
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "version": "1.0"
}
